---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Blog" description="Read website design, management, and small business marketing insights from HEX Design Labs.">
	<main class="page">
		<section class="page-hero">
			<p class="eyebrow">Blog</p>
			<h1>Notes on websites, design, and keeping business online.</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				A home for practical website guidance, maintenance tips, launch planning, and marketing notes from HEX Design Labs.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="section">
			<div class="grid">
				<article class="card blog-card blog-card-red">
					<p class="eyebrow">Coming Soon</p>
					<h3>What to update before launching a new website</h3>
					<p>A simple checklist for content, forms, analytics, search basics, and final review.</p>
				</article>
				<article class="card blog-card blog-card-green">
					<p class="eyebrow">Coming Soon</p>
					<h3>When a website refresh is enough</h3>
					<p>How to decide between a full rebuild and targeted improvements to an existing site.</p>
				</article>
				<article class="card blog-card blog-card-blue">
					<p class="eyebrow">Coming Soon</p>
					<h3>Why website maintenance matters</h3>
					<p>The small recurring tasks that keep a business website healthier over time.</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.blog-card {
		border-color: var(--blog-card-color);
		background: var(--blog-card-color);
	}

	.blog-card h3,
	.blog-card p {
		color: #ffffff;
	}

	.blog-card .eyebrow {
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82);
	}

	.blog-card-red {
		--blog-card-color: #DC4F41;
	}

	.blog-card-green {
		--blog-card-color: #ACBC3B;
	}

	.blog-card-blue {
		--blog-card-color: #54B8ED;
	}
</style>
